message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Bio-Inspired Solar Screen: an open, tested energy model for nature-inspired screens"
authors:
  - family-names: Shibli
    given-names: Shehab
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shehab6157-design/bio-inspired-solar-screen"
url: "https://shehab6157-design.github.io/bio-inspired-solar-screen/"
abstract: >-
  An open simulation model of nature-inspired screen technologies (moth-eye
  anti-glare, firefly light extraction, reflective and glowing modes, torpor
  and circadian energy planning, bee-colony task routing) for any screen
  device, validated on real satellite sunlight data, with a proposed metric,
  the Light-Life Score: energy per hour a screen is actually readable.
keywords:
  - display energy
  - biomimicry
  - energy harvesting
  - OLED
  - e-paper
  - simulation
